ap  look for him continuing his allegiance  with valentina as we learn more about  her plans  we then have the power broker who at the  end of the series  turned out to be surprise surprise  sharon carter she's given a full pardon  by the us government and the ability to  be reinstated to her old job  before going rogue to help steve rogers  this job was working with the cia but  the power broker has bigger  plans and the fact bucky and falcon  don't know she's the power broker means  that mcu isn't done with her just yet  when carly confronts sharon we get a  small glimpse at what's motivating her  to turn against the u.s  she wants vengeance towards those who  turn their back on her  and in the mid-credits scene she is on  the phone with an unknown conspirator  talking about how she'll now have access  to government secrets  prototypes and weapons but who is this  mystery person  whoever it is seems to be someone higher  up or more powerful than her i got the  feeling that she is working for this  person  valentina comes to mind zemo as well but  he's in jail and that's a bit risky  having a casual chat like this over the  phone  i think one of the craziest theories out  there is that she's talking to steve  rogers which leads me to the next  unanswered question where is steve the  last we saw him was at the end of end  game and no one seems to know where he  is  the running gag this season is that he's  living on the other side of the moon in  the original sin  comic storyline there is a space station  there where the elderly nick fury lives  and bucky eventually ends up taking over  fury's role  as the man on the wall which is the  person in charge of defending earth from  otherworldly threats  at any cost so there is a connection  between falcon in the winter soldier and  the moon  beyond those gags and with the potential  multiverse possibilities there's no  telling how cap may come back  if at all as of the writing of this  video kevin feige has said that chris  evans will not be returning to the mcu  but honestly and never say never in the  mcu we do however know there's going to  be a fourth captain america movie which  is currently in the works co-written by  malcolm spellman the creator showrunner  and head writer of falcon and the winter  soldier  nothing is known yet about this but it's  safe to assume it will start anthony  mackie  as the new captain america one person we  see very little of in the final episode  is joaquin torres  myself and many others theorized that he  would appear in the finale as the new  falcon but it seems marvel has left the  door  open too with sam taking up the mantle  as captain america this leaves the  possibility of someone stepping in  falcon shoes  and there's no one who's admired falcon  more than torres  in episode 5 sam leaves his broken  falcon suit with him  telling him to keep it so it's easy to  assume tours might reappear with this  fixed suit in either this new captain  america film  or another mcu property then there are  the flag smashers with the leaders  essentially all dead this still leaves  hundreds of thousands of their loyal  followers it's created a power vacuum of  sorts which someone could easily take  hold of  that is of course if sam's speech to the  grc members actually gets them to change  in his speech he asks the members if  they ever bothered to ask why a person  like carly  does what they do maybe if they  understand that they can change their  policies so attacks like this will never  happen  people returning from the blip has  obviously caused tremendous instability  throughout the world and how those in  power decide to hold on to it will  either result in a new antagonist taking  hold or the dismantling of the flag  smashers altogether but with the  symbolism of the mask alone on the  pavement combined with sam's speech  it's most likely we're done with the  flag smashers next up is the super  soldier serum  according to carly all the vials have  been destroyed and with the serum's  creator dr  nagel killed in episode 3 along with the  deaths of the soldiers who took the  serum  the only two people left who have super  soldier blood are john walker and isaiah  bradley i mean there is a flag smasher  who fell into the hudson that falcon has  asked to save the other end but it's not  confirmed if it's one of the super  soldier flag smashers  remember that isaiah bradley was tested  on for years by scientists to extract  this super soldier serum  so it's possible with john walker still  alive a similar thing could happen  i'd say we're done with the super  soldier serum storyline for now but i'll  keep it on my radar so we kind of figure  out what direction falcon's story is  going as he learns to take on the  responsibility of being captain america  but what about bucky he leaves his book  of amends with his therapist dr raynor  after telling his neighbor yori he  killed his son while he was the winter  soldier  all the names are crossed off he leaves  a note saying he  finished the book a notebook which used  to be steve's bucky's future is  completely open here he could team up  with falcon again  go back to wakanda or even be  manipulated by sharon in helping her out  the possibilities for him are  endless his character is pretty well  liked in the mcu so i wouldn't count on  this being the last we see him and last  but not least sam and sarah's shrimp  boat you think a guy who fought thanos  and brought down the flag smashers would  be able to get a bank loan to save his  family business well it's a pretty  jovial ending as they celebrate so i  think the business will be just fine  maybe with cap's new role he won't have  to worry about paying the bills  so those were my biggest unanswered  questions about the series what do you  think and what are your thoughts  make sure to like and subscribe and  leave a message below for more bad takes  you can follow me on twitter and  instagram  at thingstoryt until n